      "description": "TransMontaigne Partners LLC is a Denver-based U.S. midstream infrastructure platform providing terminaling, storage, transportation, blending and related logistics for refined petroleum products, renewable fuels and feedstocks, crude oil, chemicals, fertilizers and other bulk liquids. Its network spans 54 terminal facilities across major U.S. markets. ArcLight acquired platform control through the general partner in February 2016, and ArcLight Energy Partners Fund VI completed the take-private in February 2019. TLP Finance Holdings now owns 100% of TransMontaigne and is an indirect wholly owned Fund VI subsidiary. Pike Holdings and Pike Petroleum Holdings are upstream sponsor-shell census labels, not separate PortCos; intermediate holding vehicles, operating subsidiaries and individual assets beneath TransMontaigne are subsumed. No platform-level sale or signed pending ownership transfer was identified through August 15, 2026.",
